# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 1 — CONTROL Q5: the NEGATIVE control for Q4.
#
# Q4's guarded star, reached from a holder that has NO residual — it wants the WHOLE run.
# The guard reserves a trailing `"a"` that nobody claims, so the parse cannot consume the
# input at all.
#
# REQUIRED VERDICT: REJECT on "aaa" (`q5b_unguarded_control.ebnf` is the same grammar with
# the guard removed and MUST accept the same input — the one-difference pair).
#
# ⛔⛔ WHAT IT PINS. A stop-guard is CONTEXT-DEPENDENT: `constant_primary` must reserve the
# trailing `' ( … )` when it is reached from `cast`, and must NOT reserve it when it is
# reached from an ordinary expression. A guard written onto the RULE therefore cannot be
# right in both places — it has to be written onto the CALL SITE, which for this pass means
# a sheared clone reached only from the holder. The `.13` eliminator already clones; this
# says the clone is where the guard belongs.
@entry: true
scratch := star_rule
star_rule := ( "a" &"a" )*
